    thinking: "**Examining Dependencies**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a decent grasp of the initial dependencies: `express`, `@google/genai`, `motion`, and more are already in place. The main thing I\'m doing now is updating the `package.json` scripts. I\'ve switched to `tsx server.ts` for development.\n\n\n**Defining Core Mechanics**\n\nNow, I\'m diving deep into the core mechanics. I am mapping repo signals to the pet\'s state. I\'ve broken down \"health\" into percentages for easy understanding. I am focusing on the pet\'s behavior for different states like \"Behind Remote\" (leash pulling), \"Unpushed Work\" (backpack), and more.\n\n\n**Outlining Feature Sets**\n\nI\'m now outlining key feature sets to integrate. This involves structuring around clean commit streaks, verified sync statuses, and safe branch handoffs. I\'m focusing on user interaction with the pet\'s behaviors. My current focus is on building an idle repository awareness by building a compact top bar which highlights the pet name, repository name, branch selector, sync status and practice badges.\n\n\n\n**Developing Conversational UI**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the conversational UI. I\'ve fleshed out scenarios for a detached HEAD with a lost compass emotion and a stale branch with a sleepy, dusty vibe. I have added chips for quick actions like \"What needs attention?\" and \"Status report!\" I am planning a chat stream powered by Gemini API, with confidence ratings and rollback steps.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 549736720
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
