  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining App Architecture**\n\nI\'m now structuring the GitPet app\'s core architecture. Key data types, like repository health status (Healthy, Attention, Blocked, Unsafe) and symptoms (behind_remote, needing a pull), are clearly defined within `/src/types.ts`. This foundational step aims for clarity and maintainability from the outset. I am focusing on making sure data types and structures are easy to use.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Models**\n\nI\'ve fleshed out the data models. I\'m visualizing repository states, branch data like `aheadCount` and `behindCount`, and working tree files with detailed statuses. I\'ve designed action models with `command`, `confidence`, and `risk` levels, alongside stats like clean commit streaks and branch stewardship.\n\n\n**Developing Chat Interaction**\n\nI\'m solidifying the chat message model now. I\'ve defined fields like `id`, `sender`, `timestamp`, `text`, `actionCard`, `evidenceSummary`, and `isTyping`. Additionally, I\'ve created pre-configured scenarios for demos and hackathons, encompassing common Git states like sync conflicts, merge issues, detached HEADs, and stale branches, including a pristine state.\n\n**Implementing API Endpoint**\n\nThe backend is coming together, specifically focusing on the `/api/gitpet/analyze` endpoint. I am using `@google/genai` to integrate with Gemini, leveraging `gemini-3.7-flash` for AI-powered analysis. It\'ll receive repository data and user input, generating structured explanations, recommended actions, supporting evidence, confidence levels, and possible reversals. A structured generation fallback is also in place.\n\n\n**Designing Frontend Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the frontend components. I\'ve broken down the design into `Header / TopBar` and `PetStage / CanvasPet`. The `Header` includes essential repository and branch information, and interaction. The `PetStage` will feature an animated SVG avatar named \"Byte the GitPet,\" dynamically adapting its appearance to the repository\'s status. I\'ve designed several animations for various states, and interactive reactions.\n\n\n**Refining Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now incorporating sound and haptic feedback to enhance user interaction and mood perception. I\'m building out a health meter, as well as a symptom status bar. The chat stream includes a chat log with quick prompts, along with structured response rendering with high-contrast typography, evidence chips, and confidence badges. The approval gate action card features clear command previews, evidence citations, risk assessments, and a \"Preview Changes\" modal. I am including a reversal guarantee and a \"Confirm & Tidy\" button.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 269652885
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
