    thinking: "**Listing UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on the interactive UI elements. I\'ve begun by identifying and listing the necessary components. So far, I\'ve defined `src/components/TopBar.tsx`, which will contain the repository name with a clear breadcrumb and a branch badge. Next, I\'ll elaborate on the functionality within that top bar component.\n\n\n**Elaborating UI Functions**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the functionality of the UI components, specifically the dropdown for branch switching and its implications. I am now working on the health status chip, ahead/behind indicators, and a clean commit streak counter with a flame badge. I also need to flesh out the practice badges dropdown/popover, the \"90-sec Demo / Pitch Deck\" button, and the \"Repository Drawer\" toggle button. Finally, I will begin work on the `PetStage` component with the animated GitPet.\n\n\n**Defining Chat Stream**\n\nI\'ve moved on to designing the `ChatStream` component now. I\'m focusing on the emotional state chip, incorporating elements like \"Uneasy\" or \"Playful\" with visual cues, and the Health Bar, with smooth transitions and operator tooltips. I\'m also planning interactive petting/click reactions with floating hearts and animations. I\'m prioritizing the chat stream\'s interactive elements and starter chips to facilitate user interaction.\n\n\n**Designing Approval Gate**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the \"Confirm & Tidy\" approval gate button. I\'m planning a multi-step execution indicator for actions like stashing, pulling, and popping the stash, leading to a visual celebration with confetti and a health state transition to 100% healthy. I also need to begin working on the `PreviewChangesModal` component, which will contain a visualizer for branch movement, file diffs, a checklist, and a reversal guarantee.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 17
      nanos: 182125386
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
