  planner_response {
    response: "I have implemented **GitPet**, an ambient repository management companion that visualizes Git health through expressive pet states, evidence-based AI guidance, and human-approved safe actions.\n\n### What Was Built\n\n- **Expressive Pet State & Ambient Canvas**:\n  - **Dynamic Posture & Symptoms**: Animated avatar (\"Byte\") that shifts postures according to repository conditions \342\200\224 pulling forward on a leash when behind upstream, carrying a heavy backpack when holding unpushed commits, tangling in red yarn during merge conflicts, wearing a dusty nightcap when on stale merged branches, and looking lost with a spinning compass during detached HEAD states.\n  - **Ambient Aura & Health Meter**: Real-time 0\342\200\223100% health calculation with reactive glowing aura states (emerald glow for Healthy, amber pulse for Attention, and crimson pulse for Blocked).\n  - **Interactive Tactile Petting**: Click Byte anytime to pet and receive ambient purr and heart animations.\n\n- **Conversational Repository Guidance**:\n  - **Evidence-Based Explanations**: Diagnoses branch divergence in plain English, citing exact behind commit counts, affected file paths, and potential conflict markers.\n  - **AI Integration with Fallback**: Full-stack API endpoint powered by Gemini 3.7 Flash with a deterministic fallback engine.\n\n- **Human-Approved Action Gate**:\n  - **Bounded & Reversible Action Cards**: Formulates clear Git commands with explicit confidence ratings, risk badges, expected results, and guaranteed rollback commands (`git stash pop`, `git rebase --abort`).\n  - **Pre-Action Diff Preview Modal**: Inspects line-by-line file diffs, branch pointer trajectories, and atomic step plans before approval.\n  - **\"Confirm & Tidy\" Execution**: Multi-step execution progress indicator followed by state recalculation and celebratory streak confetti.\n\n- **Repository Matrix & Sandbox Testing**:\n  - **6 Deterministic Scenarios**: Including the **Hackathon MVP Scenario** (3 commits behind upstream with 2 local uncommitted files), Merge Conflict, Unpushed Commits, Detached HEAD, Stale Merged Branch, and Clean Sync.\n  - **Anomaly Injector**: One-click buttons to inject remote commits, create local uncommitted diffs, trigger conflict markers, or reset synchronization.\n\n- **Practice Streaks & Repository Drawer**:\n  - **Habit Formation**: Tracks Clean Commit streaks, Verified Sync counts, and Branch Stewardship badges.\n  - **Repository Drawer**: Slide-over panel featuring a visual branch divergence graph, working tree file inspector with diffs, stash stack browser, and an action audit log with one-click rollback.\n\n- **Pitch Deck & 90-Second Demo Guide**:\n  - Built-in 5-slide hackathon pitch deck and an interactive 4-step live demo runner to rehearse the complete *Notice \342\206\222 Understand \342\206\222 Resolve* loop in under 90 seconds."
    modified_response: "I have implemented **GitPet**, an ambient repository management companion that visualizes Git health through expressive pet states, evidence-based AI guidance, and human-approved safe actions.\n\n### What Was Built\n\n- **Expressive Pet State & Ambient Canvas**:\n  - **Dynamic Posture & Symptoms**: Animated avatar (\"Byte\") that shifts postures according to repository conditions \342\200\224 pulling forward on a leash when behind upstream, carrying a heavy backpack when holding unpushed commits, tangling in red yarn during merge conflicts, wearing a dusty nightcap when on stale merged branches, and looking lost with a spinning compass during detached HEAD states.\n  - **Ambient Aura & Health Meter**: Real-time 0\342\200\223100% health calculation with reactive glowing aura states (emerald glow for Healthy, amber pulse for Attention, and crimson pulse for Blocked).\n  - **Interactive Tactile Petting**: Click Byte anytime to pet and receive ambient purr and heart animations.\n\n- **Conversational Repository Guidance**:\n  - **Evidence-Based Explanations**: Diagnoses branch divergence in plain English, citing exact behind commit counts, affected file paths, and potential conflict markers.\n  - **AI Integration with Fallback**: Full-stack API endpoint powered by Gemini 3.7 Flash with a deterministic fallback engine.\n\n- **Human-Approved Action Gate**:\n  - **Bounded & Reversible Action Cards**: Formulates clear Git commands with explicit confidence ratings, risk badges, expected results, and guaranteed rollback commands (`git stash pop`, `git rebase --abort`).\n  - **Pre-Action Diff Preview Modal**: Inspects line-by-line file diffs, branch pointer trajectories, and atomic step plans before approval.\n  - **\"Confirm & Tidy\" Execution**: Multi-step execution progress indicator followed by state recalculation and celebratory streak confetti.\n\n- **Repository Matrix & Sandbox Testing**:\n  - **6 Deterministic Scenarios**: Including the **Hackathon MVP Scenario** (3 commits behind upstream with 2 local uncommitted files), Merge Conflict, Unpushed Commits, Detached HEAD, Stale Merged Branch, and Clean Sync.\n  - **Anomaly Injector**: One-click buttons to inject remote commits, create local uncommitted diffs, trigger conflict markers, or reset synchronization.\n\n- **Practice Streaks & Repository Drawer**:\n  - **Habit Formation**: Tracks Clean Commit streaks, Verified Sync counts, and Branch Stewardship badges.\n  - **Repository Drawer**: Slide-over panel featuring a visual branch divergence graph, working tree file inspector with diffs, stash stack browser, and an action audit log with one-click rollback.\n\n- **Pitch Deck & 90-Second Demo Guide**:\n  - Built-in 5-slide hackathon pitch deck and an interactive 4-step live demo runner to rehearse the complete *Notice \342\206\222 Understand \342\206\222 Resolve* loop in under 90 seconds."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
