  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'ve been examining the necessary API endpoints for the chatbot in `server.ts`. Currently, my focus is on the multi-turn chat history for `/api/chat`, ensuring it correctly handles both user and model messages in the history. I\'m also delving into the system instructions aspect, specifically how the roles are structured. I am thinking this will influence the implementation of the system and models.\n\n\n**Considering New Architectures**\n\nI\'m now contemplating several architectural roles for the chatbot, envisioning a team consisting of a mascot, a senior architect, a safety auditor, and a git tutor. This diverse team structure aims to provide a robust and well-rounded solution. I\'m also examining the model selection strategy, mapping specific models like `gemini-3.1-pro-preview`, `gemini-3.5-flash`, and `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` to different task complexities and desired response speeds to streamline performance. Additionally, I\'m thinking about structured responses.\n\n\n**Defining Image Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now detailing image endpoint specifications. I\'ve got `aspectRatio` and `imageSize` parameters for image generation, with base64 data URIs as output. For image editing, I\'m using `POST /api/images/edit` with `imageBase64`, prompt, and aspect ratio as inputs. The response is also a base64 data URI.\n\n**Establishing Voice Communication**\n\nI\'m architecting the voice conversation endpoint, thinking it will be a WebSocket `/live` connection linked to the Express server. The endpoint will use `gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview`, and `responseModalities` includes audio. The `systemInstruction` will be \"You are Byte, an energetic and intelligent Git companion...\". I\'m structuring this as bridging real-time audio from mic to Live API, and back to the browser via WebSocket.\n\n\n**Envisioning UI Enhancements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on UI/UX enhancements. I\'ve outlined new UI elements, including quick action tabs for features like avatar creation and live voice mode, and a persona/model switcher within the chat interface. I\'m aiming for enhanced chat streams with role tags, model tier selectors, and quick-action buttons for TTS. Plus, customizing the mascot\'s avatar, enabling quick voice chat and designing a studio modal for generating images for the avatar and various other fun images.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 965794615
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
