    thinking: "**Defining Server Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on defining the initial components needed in `server.ts`. I\'ve outlined the necessary imports, starting with `http` and `ws` for server and WebSocket functionality. The plan also includes `GoogleGenAI` from `@google/genai`. I\'m also planning the multi-turn chat API endpoint.\n\n\n**Analyzing API Parameters**\n\nI\'ve been examining the API parameters, especially the `messages`, `state`, `role`, and `tier` inputs. I\'m strategizing how to handle model selection based on the `tier` parameter, aiming for a flexible system. The plan is to map user requests to specific Gemini models based on the tier. I\'m also carefully crafting system instructions for each persona to ensure consistent behaviors: Byte, the mascot; the senior architect; and others.\n\n\n**Refining API Personas**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into refining the system instructions for each persona. The focus is on the `safety_auditor`, ensuring it can accurately assess potential risks associated with Git commands like `ancestors`, `tree hashes`, `fast-forward vs merge`, and `rebases`, emphasizing data integrity and recovery strategies. I\'m also revising the `git_tutor` persona to provide clear explanations and conceptual analogies.\nI\'ve outlined an image creation API, including prompt, aspect ratio, and size parameters. I\'ll be using `gemini-3.1-flash-image` and have a fallback for scenarios where the API key is unavailable.\n\n\n**Developing New API Endpoints**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on two new API endpoints: image editing and text-to-speech. For the image edit API, I\'m setting up a `POST /api/images/edit` endpoint. This will use the `gemini-3.1-flash-image` model. Also, I\'m defining a text-to-speech API (`POST /api/voice/tts`), that\'s going to utilize `gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview` and configure voice options. Finally, I\'ve got a plan for a real-time live API WebSocket, which will be accessible at `/live`.\n\n\n"
